      "symptom": "17 original resource/positive-startup verifications Failed at typeResolutions[0].rawJson with missing=[], unknown=[r02]. Raw native type-info includes the known versioned R02 extension; the OFF resource and negative startup controls have distinct results.",
      "reproduction": [
        "Use the exact source tuple and one original batch-P invocation retained in /Users/ah/GitHub/hybridclr/r03-local-validation/Preflight-R03LocalBatch-20261006P-lo-repair/runner-exit.json. It has already executed; do not retry P or use an old app.",
        "Read the raw files and exact fresh Player command receipts listed in FAILED_CONTRACT_REPRODUCTION.json. m07_results.verify_case reaches verify_type_resolutions, which calls m05_results.verify_type_info directly on the original native rawJson.",
        "The legacy checker accepts exactly18 fields, so the current19th r02 object raises the preserved unknown-member error. The original strict verifier reproduces each failure offline; R02_SCHEMA_DRIFT_DIAGNOSIS separately validates known33-field extension/legacy18-field types without callback substitution or raw/result rewrites."
      ],
      "relevantExcerpt": "```text\n.typeResolutions[0].rawJson: missing/unknown members: missing=[], unknown=['r02']\nm07_results.verify_type_resolutions -> m05_results.verify_type_info\nTYPE_INFO_FIELDS: original18 fields; native AppendDiagnostics emits optional r02\nR02/type_resolution_schema.py: current_m07_schema validates exact33-field extension before in-memory legacy projection\n```",
      "rootCause": "legacy_runtime invokes the unchanged M07 verifier directly for current native ON resource cases and positive startup witnesses. It does not enter the existing current_m07_schema bridge already used by R02/verify_regressions.py. Current native AssemblyShadowTypeResolver appends the known R02 object, and the managed parser supports it, but the original strict legacy Python schema deliberately rejects that extra field.",
      "whyDesignAllowedIt": "Completion copied legacy verifier entry points without the current-provider schema adapter. Earlier codec-context errors stopped these paths before type-info checks, so prior failures masked the unintegrated extension boundary.",
      "affectedScope": "All13 ON resource cases and four positive startup cases; resource-contracts is Blocked by these failures. Source/codec binding, Player execution/raw output and earlier checks are not promoted to complete M07 acceptance. Measurements and expected-negative controls retain their original independent verdicts.",
      "recommendedDirection": "Wire the existing strict current-R02 bridge (or an equivalent explicit versioned consumer) into every affected completion M07/resource and positive-startup path. Validate exact33-field schema/types/UInt64/profile/coverage, then delegate unchanged legacy semantics using an in-memory projection. Retain raw strings/files/hashes, duplicate/unknown/missing-field rejection, profile2 requirements and default legacy behavior; do not merely allow arbitrary extra fields or rewrite evidence.",
      "remainingUncertainty": "The complete M07 verifier stops at the first type-info boundary. Later resource assertions have not passed in this batch and may reveal further problems after Primary integrates the bridge; the limited schema diagnosis cannot establish full runtime acceptance.",
      "validationAfterRepair": "Add current-native raw-JSON integration tests covering all affected call paths plus missing/duplicate/unknown/mistyped extension members, UInt64 limits, profile/coverage errors, OFF behavior and raw byte custody. Run a new unused source-bound complete batch covering all13 ON resources/four positive startup witnesses and existing negative controls. Do not reclassify P.",
